{"name":"Santa Fe","hex":"#b16d52","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Santa Fe","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Places in Argentina:\nA province in the center-east of Argentina.\nThe capital city of the province of Santa Fe, Argentina; in full, Santa Fe de la Vera Cruz.","A province in the center-east of Argentina."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Santa_Fe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Santa Fe, Argentina","blocks":[{"text":"Santa Fe de la Vera Cruz, usually called just Santa Fe, is the capital city of the province of Santa Fe, Argentina. It is situated in north-eastern Argentina, near the junction of the Paraná and Salado rivers. It lies 15 kilometres (9.3 mi) from the Hernandarias Subfluvial Tunnel that connects it to the city of Paraná. The city is also connected by canal with the port of Colastiné on the Paraná River. Santa Fe de la Vera Cruz has about 423,212 people per the 2018 census [INDEC]. The metropolitan area has a population of 653,073, making it the eighth largest in Argentina."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Santa_Fe%2C_Argentina_2019_%28letras%29.jpg/330px-Santa_Fe%2C_Argentina_2019_%28letras%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Fe%2C_Argentina"},{"title":"Santa Fe Province","blocks":[{"text":"Santa Fe, officially Province of Santa Fe is a province of Argentina, located in the center-east of the country. Neighboring provinces are from the north clockwise Chaco, Corrientes, Entre Ríos, Buenos Aires, Córdoba, and Santiago del Estero. Together with Córdoba and Entre Ríos, the province is part of the economico-political association known as the Center Region."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/National_Flag_Memorial.jpg/330px-National_Flag_Memorial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Fe_Province"},{"title":"Santa Claus","blocks":[{"text":"Santa Claus is a legendary figure originating in Western Christian culture who is said to bring gifts during the late evening and overnight hours on Christmas Eve. Christmas elves are said to make the gifts in Santa's workshop, while flying reindeer pull his sleigh through the air."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Merry_Old_Santa_Claus_by_Thomas_Nast.jpg/330px-Merry_Old_Santa_Claus_by_Thomas_Nast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Claus"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Catedral_Metropolitana_Todos_los_Santos.jpg/500px-Catedral_Metropolitana_Todos_los_Santos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Catedral_Metropolitana_Todos_los_Santos.jpg/500px-Catedral_Metropolitana_Todos_los_Santos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACatedral_Metropolitana_Todos_los_Santos.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Pilares_Fundamentales_-_Joaqu%C3%ADn_Jes%C3%BAs_M%C3%A1ntaras_1.jpg/500px-Pilares_Fundamentales_-_Joaqu%C3%ADn_Jes%C3%BAs_M%C3%A1ntaras_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Pilares_Fundamentales_-_Joaqu%C3%ADn_Jes%C3%BAs_M%C3%A1ntaras_1.jpg/500px-Pilares_Fundamentales_-_Joaqu%C3%ADn_Jes%C3%BAs_M%C3%A1ntaras_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APilares_Fundamentales_-_Joaqu%C3%ADn_Jes%C3%BAs_M%C3%A1ntaras_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/02_Facultad_de_Ciencias_Jur%C3%ADdicas_y_So